        "solution": {
          "status": "ambiguous",
          "reasoning": "I is true because y'(0)=3-3=0. Applying L'Hopital's rule, the slope limit is lim_{\\theta\\to0}(-6\\sin(2\\theta)+3\\sin\\theta)/(3\\cos\\theta-6\\cos(2\\theta))=0/(-3)=0, so II is true. This gives a horizontal tangent at the cusp, making III true. The supplied worked solution concerns a different question; Math Academy's answer for this question is not captured.",
