        "solution": {
          "status": "ambiguous",
          "reasoning": "I is true: x'(3\\pi/2)=\\cos(3\\pi)+\\cos(6\\pi)=-1+1=0. With t=\\theta-3\\pi/2, x'(\\theta)\\sim-6t^2 and y'(\\theta)\\sim4t, so dy/dx\\sim-2/(3t). The left-hand limit is +\\infty, proving II; the right-hand limit is -\\infty, establishing a vertical tangent and III. The supplied worked solution addresses a different curve, so Math Academy's answer to the current question is not captured.",
