        "solution": {
          "status": "ambiguous",
          "reasoning": "I is true because x'(0)=3\\sin0\\sin0=0. Near zero, x'(\\theta)\\sim24\\theta^2 and y'(\\theta)\\sim32\\theta^3, so dy/dx\\sim4\\theta/3\\to0. Thus II is false, and the tangent is horizontal rather than vertical, making III false. The supplied worked solution concerns a different question; Math Academy's answer for the current question is not captured.",
          "confidence": 1,
          "answers": [
